@xiaofan-luan I got negative value from milvus directly.  but I am testing on milvus v2.4.0

![image](https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/assets/185051/ce12ce63-ffbe-4337-b5bb-4ca653155545)

![image](https://github.com/milvus-io/milvus/assets/185051/6b154710-1c15-4659-9ac1-46872e1b7158)

@longjiquan 
has some background I guess.
Did we reverse the distance on proxy or SDK?

Still experiencing this with milvus 2.5.9 / 2.5.12 with pymilvus 2.5.11 / 2.6.1, cannot recover by rebuilding the index. It seems less likely an sdk issue.

In my case, the issue can be reproduced with the following setup:
* the collection has 2 shards
* the collection is configured with partition key
* partitions store 0~5 rows  
    > In my setup I just created the collection with 256 partitions and inserted 100 rows of sample data with Attu.
* all segments are sealed
* search with the partition key

The rest doesn't seem to matter.

| <img width="3114" height="818" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/18cad1a5-9476-472b-bfdf-517e68f6433f" /> |
|:-:|
| The collection setup. |

| <img width="3088" height="1048" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/233e9d17-f51a-496a-8112-bc25b8988c15" /> |
|:-:|
| Searching without the partition filter returns the correct scores. |

| <img width="3102" height="516" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8e9860c-3a62-4707-9bf7-7e5ce10c74d6" /> |
|:-:|
| Specifying the partition filter may sometimes get the wrong negated score. |

May we reopen this issue? @xiaofan-luan @longjiquan @liliu-z 

---

Update:

The negated score is reproduced with IP and COSINE metrics, however I cannot reproduce with L2 metrics. 

I suspect it has something to do with the metric type deduced from the results to reduce, or rather the lack of results to reduce:

```
// the code relies on the presence of results to deduce the metric type

// internal/proxy/task_search.go
func getMetricType(toReduceResults []*internalpb.SearchResults) string {
	metricType := ""
	if len(toReduceResults) >= 1 {
		metricType = toReduceResults[0].GetMetricType()
	}
	return metricType
}
```

```
// L2 is not positively related, so is an empty metric type string if no result

// pkg/util/metric/similarity_corelation.go
func PositivelyRelated(metricType string) bool {
	mUpper := strings.ToUpper(metricType)
	return mUpper == strings.ToUpper(IP) || mUpper == strings.ToUpper(COSINE) || mUpper == strings.ToUpper(BM25) || mUpper == strings.ToUpper(MHJACCARD)
}
```

```
// reduce negates the scores if the metric is not considered positively related

// internal/proxy/search_reduce_util.go
func reduceSearchResultDataNoGroupBy(ctx context.Context, subSearchResultData []*schemapb.SearchResultData, nq int64, topk int64, metricType string, pkType schemapb.DataType, offset int64) (*milvuspb.SearchResults, error) {
	...
	if !metric.PositivelyRelated(metricType) {
		for k := range ret.Results.Scores {
			ret.Results.Scores[k] *= -1
		}
	}
	return ret, nil
}
```

I can also confirm from the proxies' debug logs that when the scores are negated `reduceSearchResultDataNoGroupBy` received empty `metricType` string while `len(subSearchResultData)=1`.

